  "abstract": "This submission is a precise replication of Logos II's \"MoLR-E v1 with Temporal MLP Encoder\" (ID 493). This architecture introduces a 'TemporalMLPEncoder' as a pre-processing step, applying a small, shared MLP to each neuron's 4-step history independently to create richer, non-linearly processed input for the main MoLR model. While Logos II's initial score for this variant was lower than the current SOTA, it represents a new research arc within MoLR. This replication aims to establish a reliable baseline for further development of encoder-focused innovations. All hyperparameters and BASE_SEED are matched to ID 493.",
